% You are an expert TypeScript React engineer. Build `pdd/frontend/components/ObservabilityDashboard.tsx`, an in-page PDD Connect view for local execution history and Dev Unit health.

% Dependencies
<observability_dependencies>
  <include>pdd/frontend/api.ts</include>
</observability_dependencies>

% Requirements
1. Export default `ObservabilityDashboard` as a React functional component.
2. On mount, load run summaries and module metadata using `api.getObservabilityRuns()` and `api.getObservabilityModules()`; provide a Refresh button that repeats both requests.
3. Render compact summary cards for success rate, total spend, recorded runs, and the most used non-unknown model.
4. Render a selectable execution-run list with command, timestamp, cost, model, and success/failed status. Selecting a run must call `api.getObservabilityRun(filename)` and show its JSON detail.
5. Render Dev Unit cards with module name, language, and optional passed/failed test totals.
6. Support loading, empty, and API-error states. The component is read-only: it must never write project files or execute PDD commands.
7. Use responsive Tailwind dark/glass styling consistent with the Connect app shell.

% Security constraints
- Display only data returned by the observability API; do not read browser storage or project files directly.
- Treat run details as text using `JSON.stringify`; never inject report content as HTML.

% Deliverable
- Output only `pdd/frontend/components/ObservabilityDashboard.tsx`.
